# Git push at end of work

When you finish a task that changed files in this repository:

1. Run `git status` — if there are no changes, skip commit/push.
2. Stage only relevant files (never `.env`, credentials, or secrets).
3. Commit with a clear message (use HEREDOC for the message body).
4. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).
5. Tell the user the commit hash and that GitHub Pages redeploys in ~3–5 minutes.

Use commit author from the latest commit if git user identity is not configured:

`GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Victor Gutierrez" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="VictorHGutierrez-cloud@users.noreply.github.com"` (and same for `GIT_COMMITTER_*`).

Do not skip push unless the user explicitly says not to push, or push would fail without credentials (then explain what they need to run).
